{"kind":"report","text":"Changes requested: exact M8 head 471399bafb62c93a353ecdd43fdc15f8fc450f20 on builder/typed-core-m8-20261107, tree edb98fe8, all 106 paths, for request bd1a9429 under promise 689c9fd1 and review request 63acda6f. Production holds. An independent read of every body route finds no behavior change for an admitted definition. The two body seals are the parser's real output, the full gate passes and the Page workflow passes. One test-only change is required, F1 below. It needs no new full gate, Page workflow or seal review.\n\nF1 (blocks; test-only). Six cases in packages/derive/test/program.test.ts no longer compare a full result with production behavior. On main, `agree()` ran the prototype and production `derive` on the same input and required equal `Ran` values. The partial `toMatchObject` checks in those cases rested on that equality. At the head, `expected` comes from `executeBody`, and `evaluate` runs `evaluateAdmitted`, which calls the same `executeBody`. `agree()` therefore now proves only that observation leaves the result unchanged. The six partial checks are at lines 115, 119, 138, 239, 249 and 250, in these cases:\n- \"a tell tests the before state, reads the working payload, and skips no ordinal\"\n- \"an absent source leaves the default and an explicit clear records null\"\n- \"preparation collects once, unavailable does not hide a later false guard, and structural time includes skipped reads\"\n- \"the structural visitor includes skipped clock reads and the complete opaque input\"\n\nFor those bodies, no test at the head checks the full `Ran` against main. Ruling 24e2a8d1 says to keep every literal full `Ran` outcome. The retirement ledger says \"The complete literal keeps\" for the first of those cases, but that case matches only part of its result.\n\nRequired change: replace each of the six checks with the full `Ran` literal. Take each literal from main cdd5508c's production `derive` for the same input, and keep that comparison in the evidence. Correct the ledger row. Under docs/testing.md this is a test-only follow-up. Run the derive test compiler context and the complete program.test.ts owner once.\n\nWhat holds:\n\n- Scope. Main cdd5508c is an ancestor, the head is pushed, and the builder's worktree is clean at the head. Against main, the head changes exactly the 106 paths that its artifacts cover:\n  - 101 files have one artifact each.\n  - Directory artifact d9548286 covers the five deleted prototype files.\n  - The commit-message check passes: 58 checked, 0 flagged.\n  - No dependency, lockfile, gate script, workflow or Wrangler file changes.\n- Retirements. Live artifacts exist on the five deleted paths: model.ts c856e4db, lower.ts f962e958, evaluate.ts 59dade20, explain.ts 27c444b5 and dependencies.ts 615326f5. The gitseq merge rules retire each with no successor and give the directory its successor. Six files under program/ stay unchanged, and their live artifacts must stay live: capability-plan.ts, condition-plan.ts, condition-value.ts, effect-plan.ts, send-plan.ts and settlement.ts. I will check the receipt for exactly that.\n- The seals. genesis.ts and judge.ts have not changed since 5b47520c. I recomputed both outside the builder's worktree with the test's own parser:\n  - Main gives 35478847… and 89d7601f….\n  - The head gives 15a4adb0… and 7bafa496….\n  - Only those two literals change in scripts/security-entry-points.test.mjs.\n- What the sealed sources change:\n  - Both files read declarations through `declarationOf(definition)`, which throws for an unadmitted definition. Main read `definition.declared`.\n  - genesis.ts runs the named admitted act body with the same seed cause, first ordinal and directory. The validator requires an open genesis, so the runner opens `act.on`.\n  - actJudged runs the named act body, which opens an item only for an open step.\n  - In judgeTimed, the operation-owner policy moves into the runner with the same five pins, scope kind, owner choice