endencies. The archive schema cache key equals the validator's uniqueness key for handlers, and only the constructor fills it.\n\nNotes (no change required):\n\n1. Some lookups still return an empty value on a miss. `nativeOutcomes` returns `{}` for an unadmitted definition (program/native.ts line 131), and settle.ts line 219 now uses it. `itemSettlementBinding` returns null, as on main. The unchanged catch in scope/src/reads.ts line 186 now also turns a `declarationOf` throw into false. No admitted definition reaches these.\n2. `handlerBranch` returns null for any unregistered body, so runClause reports \"names no declared late branch\" (handlers.ts line 507) when no late branch was asked for.\n3. A structure failure during admission now becomes \"has no canonical bytes\" at path \"\" (validate/format-1.ts line 197). In the validator branches read, a missing guard plan always comes with a reported problem, so no definition that main admitted is refused.\n4. The ledger leaves out four test changes, though every assertion stays:\n   - forms-binding.test.ts line 514 and replay/test/view.test.ts line 100 replace the copied definition with a `View` that drops index writes. It drops that item's writes at every entry, not only at its opening.\n   - program-reads.test.ts line 218 reverses two identity checks.\n   - The second `typeObligations` check now tests only the guard site's phase literal.\n5. `evaluateAdmitted` is test-only. It gives the copy a fresh `ran`, so production must not adopt it without the clock check in runHandler.\n\nArchitecture: sound. One runner executes every admitted body family from the validation's own instructions. Explain observes that run, and Dependencies reads only the static plan. The judges keep authority, signatures, admission and journal sealing.\n\nSecurity: no finding. The two judges keep every check in its order. An unadmitted definition now stops at `declarationOf` and `nativeMark`, where M7 let it skip the founding grant rule.\n\nSimplification: no required change. Removing the prototype and the timed-array adapter leaves one runner. Notes 1 and 2 are the remaining places where a miss returns a value instead of stopping.\n\nThis verdict authorizes no landing or deployment and closes no live acceptance.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:07aaf81412253b06ce02ad666a304225606313b2","binding":"assigned","head":"471399bafb62c93a353ecdd43fdc15f8fc450f20","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:64aa62ca729cd68861e5f0548c322a7b07d9ee66\",\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:b714f108358ec1cf0c4dab7317206692c1592496\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:689c9fd1c37b67c0babca148485b7c3bbfdcafbd\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:6ea61ce4c1627169ac76759fce0c90c511aad15a","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"changes-requested"}}